From 6552401babd31df06b1b4d22d6f8fb040ccf22ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Payton <brandon@happycode.net>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:17:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 21/22] Kandelo: Use existing process and thread initialization
 paths

Initialize passive data at process instantiation. Kandelo already removes the start function from thread replicas, so each Go worker can use a dynamically placed slot in the existing shared memory.

Move off the retiring Go stack before publishing that it can be reclaimed, then call the existing kernel_exit import. The guest uses Kandelo ABI 56 and needs no new host import or thread layout marker.

